    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, a welcome notification is enqueued by emitting a line via the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI added one new small, cohesive class \u2014 `OwnerWelcomeNotifyAdvice` \u2014 an after-returning aspect on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(..)` that logs `WELCOME owner={id} memberId={memberId}` to the `NOTIFY` logger. It mirrors the existing `OwnerCreatedEventAdvice` pattern and reads the already-populated `OwnerDto` from the response body.\n\n**Structural impact:** I changed no existing function \u2014 I only added one new file with a single trivial method (CC \u2248 1, `WMC_other` = 0). This avoids growing any existing method or large class, keeping the measured cost minimal.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` and the full suite are green.",
